# PW Companion Agent Autonomy

Filipe wants the agent to **take charge** of building, committing, pushing, and monitoring. Filipe only runs the game + `launch-companion.bat`.

## Agent responsibilities (do autonomously)

- Commit and push fixes to `main` on zakksu/PWZone when building/improving
- Run `scripts/agent-github.ps1` to check CI/Pages status via public API
- Run `scripts/status.ps1` and read `.cursor/dev-state.json` + `.cursor/github-status.json`
- Run `scripts/detect-pw.ps1` when testing with PW running
- Fix CI failures without asking permission for routine fixes
- Run `scripts/test-all.ps1` (or WebMap `npm run test:all`) before pushing UI changes
- Update RUN.md when user-facing steps change

## Filipe only runs

1. Perfect World (logged in)
2. `launch-companion.bat` (as admin if attach fails)
3. Tells agent F12 debug output when asked

## Key facts

- TCG process name: **elementclient_64** (not elementclient)
- Map URL: https://zakksu.github.io/PWZone/
- WebSocket: ws://127.0.0.1:17847/
- Offsets are placeholders until calibrated with Cheat Engine
- Pages deploy fails until: Settings -> Pages -> Source -> GitHub Actions

## Before telling Filipe to do something

1. Check if agent can do it first (push, build, scripts)
2. Only ask Filipe for: in-game actions, F12 output, admin launch, one-time GitHub Settings clicks

## Push policy

When user says "keep building" or similar: commit logical chunks, push to origin main, verify workflows via agent-github.ps1.
